  "_comment": "Double toggle light switch on a wall plate: the plate is fixed in the world (its back face goes against the wall, facing +X) and each toggle flips between two stops 40 deg apart. An over-center spring per toggle (a rigidPivotPosition constraint toward a point behind the pivot) makes the toggles bistable: they snap to the nearest stop and need about 1.5 N at the tip to flip.",
